        "note": "The almost-schur implementation and its RellichKondrachov sources are vendored byte-for-byte from this immutable snapshot under vendor/almost-schur, with the original license, notices, and provenance inventories preserved. They compile as local libraries into the root .lake/build, avoiding both sibling path dependencies and the registry's Git-subdirectory sandbox bug. It supplies geometric curvature and connection constructions, integration and Bochner identities, Sobolev compactness, variational PDE, and regularity infrastructure. Its authors are Arthur Freitas Ramos, David Barros Hulak, and Ruy J. G. B. de Queiroz. The new selected result is Lichnerowicz-Obata, not the inherited almost-Schur theorem. The independent geometry vocabulary is adapted from that source, and the three Comparator/Landrun shell scripts are exact copies.",
